---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WriteInBlock from '../components/WriteInBlock.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { webPage, breadcrumb } from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/issues';
const schema = webPage({
  name: 'Issues & Platform',
  description: `Where ${site.candidate.name} stands on the issues facing ${site.candidate.office}.`,
  path,
  author: true,
  extraNodes: [
    breadcrumb([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Issues', path },
    ]),
  ],
});
---

<BaseLayout title="Issues" description={`Where ${site.candidate.name} stands on the issues facing Woodstock.`} schema={schema}>
  <section class="bg-navy text-white">
    <div class="container-narrow py-14 lg:py-20 text-center">
      <p class="text-xs font-heading font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-red mb-3">Where I stand</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-display font-extrabold text-white text-balance">Why I'm Running for {site.candidate.office}</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-white/70">In my own words.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="container-narrow py-14 lg:py-20 space-y-10 text-lg text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <p>
          When I didn't win the June primary, that experience gave me something I didn't expect: clarity.
          I've spent the past several months carrying out the full duties of the Town Clerk's office, and
          every day in that work has deepened my conviction that Woodstock deserves leadership that is
          present, honest, and genuinely accessible. That's why I'm running as a write-in candidate for
          Town Supervisor.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          I don't come to this with an agenda for one group or one side. I come to it with a love for this
          whole community and a belief that the world gets a little better when we show up honestly, trust
          our own voice, and do the work.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-display font-extrabold text-navy mb-4">Accessible Leadership</h2>
        <p>
          Leadership should be reachable. To me that means an open door, answered phone calls, and thoughtful
          responses — not eventually, but as a matter of course. Residents shouldn't have to fight to be heard
          by their own town government. As Supervisor, I want the people of Woodstock to know that when they
          reach out, someone is actually listening, and that access to their local government is the norm,
          not the exception.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-display font-extrabold text-navy mb-4">Open, Transparent Decisions</h2>
        <p>
          Trust is earned by governing in the open. I believe in leadership that communicates openly, explains
          its decisions, welcomes questions, and includes others in the decisions that affect them. Good
          government listens before it speaks and studies before it decides — and it never forgets that every
          decision touches someone's family, livelihood, or future. I'll bring that habit of explaining the
          "why," inviting scrutiny, and making the reasoning behind town decisions something residents can see
          and understand.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-display font-extrabold text-navy mb-4">Supporting the People Who Serve Woodstock</h2>
        <p>
          I believe our town employees are one of Woodstock's greatest strengths. Over the past several months
          working inside town government, I've watched departments collaborate, community organizations step
          forward, and volunteers give far more than anyone asked — not because they were told to, but because
          they care. When we trust good people, support them, and encourage collaboration, they do
          extraordinary things for our neighbors. As Supervisor, I'll lead in a way that empowers the people
          who keep this town running.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-display font-extrabold text-navy mb-4">Practical, Whole-Community Government</h2>
        <p>
          Caring is where it starts, but competence is how it gets done. For more than two decades I've worked
          in administration, business management, and bookkeeping, and I run a business that helps other
          organizations build budgets and the kind of clear, sustainable systems that let them operate
          smoothly. That's exactly the skill set a town needs in its Supervisor — someone who understands
          operations and budgets, and who can turn good intentions into government that actually works, for
          the whole community and not one corner of it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-display font-bold text-navy">
          I believe the greatest responsibility any of us can accept is caring for a place that is caring for
          us. For me, that place is Woodstock. That's why I'm asking you to write me in.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <WriteInBlock tone="light" />
</BaseLayout>
